{
  "analysis": "All three classes fail on SMALL defects: inclusion recall 0.16 (low-size tertile 0.027, n=146; missed median 37px vs train 90px), patches 0.65 (low tertile 0.40, missed 50px vs 85px), scratches 0.58 (low tertile 0.40, missed 41px vs 73px). Misses are also low-contrast. Inclusion is worst and most starved (10 real imgs, 158 misses) so it gets the largest share; patches/scratches kept fed to avoid starving the shared detector. Plan = bias every class toward small scales and small source defects to match the missed size band, while staying above the unlearnable-tiny floor (scale_min 0.4).",
  "allocation": {"inclusion": 24, "patches": 14, "scratches": 12},
  "params": {
    "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.4, "scale_max": 1.0, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [50, 100, 131, 268, 277, 287]},
    "patches": {"scale_min": 0.4, "scale_max": 0.9, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [14, 39, 63, 64, 94, 106, 161, 251]},
    "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.4, "scale_max": 0.9, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
  },
  "rationale": "Target the dominant failure mode (small, low-contrast defects) by scaling sources down into the 35-70px band that the model currently misses, using prefer_small weighting and small/medium source defects whose shape matches the misses (thin dark marks for inclusion, small dark blobs for patches, thin bright lines for scratches; rotation/flip covers orientation so all scratch sources are used). Inclusion gets the most (24) because it is far below the others and most starved, but stays well under the ~80 diminishing-return threshold; patches (14) and scratches (12) remain fed so the shared detector is not starved. same_class backgrounds keep pastes realistic (dark inclusions/blobs on matching steel, bright lines on gray steel) and avoid invisible pastes on mismatched backgrounds."
}

